A||||7||86_Fastback||Coolant leak
Z||000000||86_Fastback||06-23-99||11:42 AM||||This is my first real problem with my Fiero GT.  I noticed a coolant leak that appears to be coming from the front side of the engine (V-6).  I can not see exactly where though, but it is about the middle of the car.  Anyone have any ideas?  Is it a hose or a pipe?  Is there a freeze plug that could be causing it?  Any help would be great.  I need to get this resolved.<br>-Gregg
Z||000001||PaUL||06-23-99||02:25 PM||||Odds are its coming form the water pump bearing weephole. If it is, youll have to get a new one, fairly easy to install.
Z||000002||86_Fastback||06-23-99||05:15 PM||||Paul,<br>Are you saying I need to replace the water pump?  What steps does it take to accomplish this.
Z||000003||batboy||06-23-99||05:34 PM||||If the water pump bearings and seal get a lot of wear, they can leak. I'd try to figure out for sure where the leak is coming from first. Check to see if there is any play in the water pump shaft. Grab the pulley and try to wiggle it up and down, then back and forth. Any noticeable slop means it's time for a new water pump. Other things can leak too. I've see freeze plugs with pin-hole leaks from rusting out (although not on a Fiero). Check all the hoses too, especially the heater hoses.
Z||000004||PaUL||06-23-99||08:02 PM||||on the 2.8 waterpump there is a small hole near the pulley that weeps coolant when the bearing is worn. Its purpose is to indicate that you need to change the waterpump.
Z||000005||batboy||06-23-99||09:00 PM||||PaUL's right about the weep hole, they're on most Chevy small blocks too. Often you'll see a rusty stain leading down from this weep hole when it's been leaking for a while.
Z||000006||Bruce||06-24-99||09:25 AM||||Mine was doing the same thing a week ago- there was a leak in the coolant tube located near the air conditioning unit. I took the car in and had the tube taken out and brazed.<br>The leak I had was located a little to the left and in front of the right rear wheel.<br>I have the same model and year as you.
Z||000007||86_Fastback||06-24-99||11:29 AM||||I was able to get a closer look today.  It is coming from the front of the engine.  Somewhere above the starter is my guess.  Could not see due to the starter being in the way.  Some times it only leaks a few drops, others a small puddle.  If anyone has a schematic on the layot of all the coolant hoses and pipes it would help me.
